 "summary": "SH is a single-row wire-to-board connector family on a 1.0 mm pitch. Wires of AWG #32 to #28 are crimped into SSH contacts, which lock into SHR receptacle housings of 2 to 20 circuits; these mate with surface-mount headers, BM..B-SRSS-TB entering from the top and SM..B-SRSS-TB from the side. SM04B-SRSS-TB is the four-circuit side-entry header. Each contact carries 1.0 A at up to 50 V AC/DC over -25 to +85 °C.",
